                <pb facs="0602" n="508" sameAs="frus:frus1924v02/pg508"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">817.00/3081: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Chargé in Nicaragua</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Thurston</hi>) <hi
                        rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of
                    State</hi></head>
                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Paraphrase]</seg></opener>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Managua</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1924-06-07T09:00:00-05:45"><hi rendition="#italic">June 7, 1924—9
                                a.m.</hi></date><lb/>[Received 8:30 p.m.]</dateline></opener>
                <p>108. During interview with President last evening I informed him of the contents
                    of your 66, June 5, 5 p.m. He said he would withdraw his candidacy …</p>
                <p rendition="#center">. . . . . . . . . . . . . .</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Thurston</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
